# demo/latency.sh, six runs, QNX 8.0 on QEMU (KVM, 2 vCPUs) on WSL2, swtpm; 2026-11-27.
# 1 kHz SCHED_FIFO loop (tools/rt-probe), 30 s per row; jitter = |period - 1 ms| in microseconds.
# witnessd and the TPM driver serve attestation at priority 8; the loop runs above it (10) or below it (7).
# QEMU on a laptop: idle rows already show millisecond outliers from the host. Compare rows, not absolutes.
# Runs 5 and 6 ran while the host was busy (their idle rows degrade too, and run 5's flood reached only 14.4/s);
# they are kept, not dropped.

### run 1
1 kHz loop, 30 s per run; witnessd and the TPM driver serve attestation at priority 8
==> loop at priority 10, idle
rt-probe: priority 10, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 6 p99 132 p99.9 309 max 2568 mean 15.2; over 1 ms: 3
==> loop at priority 10, attestation flood
rt-probe: priority 10, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 12 p99 174 p99.9 994 max 1125 mean 26.4; over 1 ms: 1
  load: 679 attestations (21.2/s) from 8 clients
==> loop at priority 7, idle
rt-probe: priority 7, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 4 p99 141 p99.9 894 max 3275 mean 16.1; over 1 ms: 5
==> loop at priority 7, attestation flood
rt-probe: priority 7, 1000 Hz, 30000 wake-ups: jitter us p50 17 p99 170 p99.9 993 max 4662 mean 28.9; over 1 ms: 10
  load: 703 attestations (22.0/s) from 8 clients
